From d51d244cf9c7297e4306de2069535d26c8187395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PixelOS vegas builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:33:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] PropImitationHooks: port crDroid Play Integrity spoofing

Bring the Play Integrity handling of crDroid 16.0
(core/java/android/security/pif/PlayIntegritySpoofService.java and the
property area virtualization in core/jni/android_os_SystemProperties.cpp)
into PixelOS's PropImitationHooks:

- PIF config from Settings.Secure pif_data (user), else fetched_pif
  (AttestationService), else the overlay array; JSON or key=value format,
  Build and Build.VERSION fields with or without the VERSION. prefix,
  system properties and the PlayIntegrityFork options spoofBuild,
  spoofProps, spoofVendingBuild, spoofVendingSdk, verboseLogs.
- Missing Build fields are derived from FINGERPRINT, and
  DEVICE_INITIAL_SDK_INT from the config or the device codename.
- In com.google.android.gms.unstable the process' property areas are
  remapped copy-on-write and patched, so native and Java property reads
  see the certified fingerprint, id, product, model, security patch,
  first API level, init.svc.adbd=stopped and sys.usb.state=mtp.
- One debug log line per target process says what was applied.

Key attestation stays refused for DroidGuard through
onEngineGetCertificateChain, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
